# Windows shim for Infection's Mago static analysis tool. Infection probes for a
# `.bat` before the extensionless binary, which is the only supported way to stop
# it prefixing PHP_BINARY to a native Rust executable. Local to the machine, so
# never committed. See webinertia/webware-tools issue 59.
/mago.bat
